1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
This has nothing to do with snow.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
All-season tires stop working
around 45 degrees.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Below that, the rubber
compound stiffens up.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
And grip drops — on dry pavement
too, not just snow.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Winter tires use a softer
compound that stays flexible.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
That's the whole difference —
not the tread pattern, the rubber itself.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Save this for when
the forecast turns.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
